WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
1948.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:05.670
Two philosophers argue about
God, live on the radio.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.910
One of them, Bertrand Russell, points
out that every human has a mother,

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.430
but the human race does not.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.350
His point: what is true of each
part need not be true of the whole.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.400
So can anyone prove that God exists, or
is the most an argument can do to make

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.820
it likely?

8
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.170
In this mission, you'll sort
arguments by where they start:

9
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.390
from what we observe,
or from thought alone.

10
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.810
Then you'll map how believers and
critics link reason and faith.

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.940
Your mission: weigh up whether an
argument can prove that God exists,

12
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.670
or only make it likely.
